<!--METHOD
The figures come from the publicly posted price lists of Bratislava developers, which Residata reads daily, flat by flat. Supply is the available and reserved flats in active projects; only flats are counted, not parking, cellars or commercial units. Prices include VAT and are averaged over the flats whose price the developer publishes. Supply and price levels are the mean of the daily readings over the final two weeks of the period, so that no single day decides a figure. Projects are assigned to districts by the borough they stand in. Quarter-on-quarter changes are measured on the same panel of projects in both periods — otherwise growth in our own coverage would read as movement in the market. A sale is a flat that left a price list and did not come back; reservations are not counted as sales. Figures up to {lastPublishedEn} come from the quarterly analyses of Bencont Investments and carry their name — we do not splice them onto ours as one series.
-->
